ng that seemed pretty  believable at the time after all it's  really tom holland's spider-man movie or  at least it was  so it would make sense that he would get  most of the spotlight for most of the  film  so nobody really questioned this however  there are conflicting reports today  and these are more likely going to  happen and this is kind of a two-part  report the first part is when daniel  replied to a tweet on twitter  somebody asked him if toby is a  supporting role or a  action cameo and his reply was i heard  that from the moment they appear in the  movie toby and andrew become  co-leads to holland now this is the  report that i was talking about in the  beginning where i stated some people may  not like this  especially if you are a tom holland fan  a lot of people were kind of upset with  the doctor strange announcement when  they stated that doctor strange was  going to be appearing in spiderman no  way home as sort of a mentor for peter  parker  a lot of people were pretty upset about  this because they want tom holland  spider-man to be on his own in  spider-man homecoming he had tony stark  in civil war avengers end game and  avengers infinity war again he had tony  stark  even though he saved tony's life at one  point and in game and then in spider-man  far from home he had another mentor and  that mentor was really happy  mysterio faked it for a while and peter  was pretty happy to have him as a mentor  but of course we know how that played  out but happy brought the plane brought  the new suits gave him the pep talk  and that was fine because that was a  little bit less mentorship than he had  in the previous film and fans really  wanted to see spider-man go out on his  own in spider-man no way home but it  doesn't appear that's going to be the  case  now it looks like he's not only going to  have doctor strange but also toby  maguire spider-man  and andrew garfield spider-man as well  fighting right beside him however don't  get too upset about 